{"parentUuid":"6646f3d2-3a2e-4edf-9e2f-5ba2036d0f18","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1bf9e23bdb17aa09","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg22SJ7JRdHyaeqXRkCkF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SH6mEmHrcmJHuU6FYWDPCC","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"MultiEcuScan vLinker FS STN1170 baud rate 115200 500000 settings AlfaOBD adapter"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":136366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":879,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SH6mEmHrcmJHuU6FYWDPCC":{"query":"MultiEcuScan vLinker FS STN1170 baud rate 115200 500000 settings AlfaOBD adapter"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"55d76961-5815-4dbe-900f-2541ff636f4f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cg22SHrgP75UtRcadwehs","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"60d06b62-0b09-4b83-a802-f0d23ffad1ab","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:09:36.309Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"6646f3d2-3a2e-4edf-9e2f-5ba2036d0f18","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"a1bf9e23bdb17aa09","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QQLJ15A3FSnkQCH2M3vstk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio Giorgio Security Gateway Module AutoAuth wiTECH bypass OBD passthrough\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SGW Bypass Module Giulia Stelvio 2018+\",\"url\":\"https://centerlinealfa.com/catalog/sgw-bypass-module-giulia-stelvio-2018\"},{\"title\":\"Alfissimo SGW Bypass (Security Gateway bypass)- Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio, Maserati Ghibli, Levante, Quattroporte\",\"url\":\"https://shop.alfissimo.com/diagnostic-softwarehardware-multiecuscanalfaobd/3132-alfissimo-sgw-bypass-security-gateway-bypass-alfa-romeo-giuliastelvio-.html\"},{\"title\":\"Giulia / Stelvio Security Gateway / SGW Bypass / umgehen / ausbauen / brücken - Page 9 - ItaloEcu - Alfa Romeo Portal - Community und Forum für Alfisti - Fachforum Reparatur Werkstatt Anleitungen Technik Hilfe Tuning Beratung Verkauf Teile Ersatzteile Treffen ItaloEcu\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfa-romeo-portal.com/forum/thread/3747-giulia-stelvio-security-gateway-sgw-bypass-umgehen-ausbauen-br%C3%BCcken/?pageNo=9\"},{\"title\":\"SGW BYPASS PLUG (FCA CARS 2017+)\",\"url\":\"https://shopeurocompulsion.net/products/swg-bypass-plug-alfa-romeo-giulia-stelvio-2-0l\"},{\"title\":\"SGW BYPAS (SECURITYGATEWAYBYPASS) - ALFA ROMEO GIULIA & STELVIO\",\"url\":\"https://vulkanmotive.com/products/swg-bypass-alfa-romeo-giulia-stelivio\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"},{\"title\":\"FCA SGW MODULE\",\"url\":\"https://shopeurocompulsion.net/blogs/installation-database/fca-sgw-module-bypass-installation-info\"},{\"title\":\"SGW bypass FCA - SHOP STUFF4CAR\",\"url\":\"https://shop.stuff4car.com/en/index.php?route=product%2Fproduct&product_id=51\"},{\"title\":\"Security Gateway Bypass Module\",\"url\":\"https://www.zautomotive.com/products/z_sgw\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio Security Gateway Module:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Security Gateway Module (SGW) Bypass is designed for Giulia and Stelvio 2018+, and the Stelvio uses FCA's Giorgio platform, shared with the Giulia saloon.\n\n## Purpose and Function\n\nBeginning with model years 2018 and above Alfa Romeo vehicles are equipped with a security gateway module, designed to prevent CAN bus hacking over the G or LTE network. However, while the SGW module is designed to prevent unwanted remote access to the vehicle's CAN system, it also limits the ability to access the BCM, Infotainment system, and ECM modules for servicing or modifying the vehicle.\n\n## Bypass Capability\n\nThe SGW bypass device allows you to perform service warning resets, flash tune your vehicle, and enable/disable features via 3rd party software applications. SGW Bypass is a plug-and-play solution that unlocks full diagnostic capabilities with 3rd party OBD scan tools such as Multiscan ECU, AlfaOBD, etc.\n\n## Installation Location\n\nFor Stelvio, the location of SGW is behind instrument cluster near windshield under the dash.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nAlfa Romeo Stelvio compatibility includes NAFTA: 2.2018+/EMEA 4.2018+ production including MY2020-26.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"15799513-bd4e-4066-9c9e-de5be64dbb83","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:09:42.568Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio Giorgio Security Gateway Module AutoAuth wiTECH bypass OBD passthrough","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DRfCZbT6m1NsPXjjFH7b7C","content":[{"title":"SGW Bypass Module Giulia Stelvio 2018+","url":"https://centerlinealfa.com/catalog/sgw-bypass-module-giulia-stelvio-2018"},{"title":"Alfissimo SGW Bypass (Security Gateway bypass)- Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio, Maserati Ghibli, Levante, Quattroporte","url":"https://shop.alfissimo.com/diagnostic-softwarehardware-multiecuscanalfaobd/3132-alfissimo-sgw-bypass-security-gateway-bypass-alfa-romeo-giuliastelvio-.html"},{"title":"Giulia / Stelvio Security Gateway / SGW Bypass / umgehen / ausbauen / brücken - Page 9 - ItaloEcu - Alfa Romeo Portal - Community und Forum für Alfisti - Fachforum Reparatur Werkstatt Anleitungen Technik Hilfe Tuning Beratung Verkauf Teile Ersatzteile Treffen ItaloEcu","url":"https://www.alfa-romeo-portal.com/forum/thread/3747-giulia-stelvio-security-gateway-sgw-bypass-umgehen-ausbauen-br%C3%BCcken/?pageNo=9"},{"title":"SGW BYPASS PLUG (FCA CARS 2017+)","url":"https://shopeurocompulsion.net/products/swg-bypass-plug-alfa-romeo-giulia-stelvio-2-0l"},{"title":"SGW BYPAS (SECURITYGATEWAYBYPASS) - ALFA ROMEO GIULIA & STELVIO","url":"https://vulkanmotive.com/products/swg-bypass-alfa-romeo-giulia-stelivio"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio"},{"title":"FCA SGW MODULE","url":"https://shopeurocompulsion.net/blogs/installation-database/fca-sgw-module-bypass-installation-info"},{"title":"SGW bypass FCA - SHOP STUFF4CAR","url":"https://shop.stuff4car.com/en/index.php?route=product%2Fproduct&product_id=51"},{"title":"Security Gateway Bypass Module","url":"https://www.zautomotive.com/products/z_sgw"}]},"Based on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio Security Gateway Module:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Security Gateway Module (SGW) Bypass is designed for Giulia and Stelvio 2018+, and the Stelvio uses FCA's Giorgio platform, shared with the Giulia saloon.\n\n## Purpose and Function\n\nBeginning with model years 2018 and above Alfa Romeo vehicles are equipped with a security gateway module, designed to prevent CAN bus hacking over the G or LTE network. However, while the SGW module is designed to prevent unwanted remote access to the vehicle's CAN system, it also limits the ability to access the BCM, Infotainment system, and ECM modules for servicing or modifying the vehicle.\n\n## Bypass Capability\n\nThe SGW bypass device allows you to perform service warning resets, flash tune your vehicle, and enable/disable features via 3rd party software applications. SGW Bypass is a plug-and-play solution that unlocks full diagnostic capabilities with 3rd party OBD scan tools such as Multiscan ECU, AlfaOBD, etc.\n\n## Installation Location\n\nFor Stelvio, the location of SGW is behind instrument cluster near windshield under the dash.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nAlfa Romeo Stelvio compatibility includes NAFTA: 2.2018+/EMEA 4.2018+ production including MY2020-26."],"durationSeconds":6.820083800077438,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"55d76961-5815-4dbe-900f-2541ff636f4f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6646f3d2-3a2e-4edf-9e2f-5ba2036d0f18","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"60d06b62-0b09-4b83-a802-f0d23ffad1ab","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"a1bf9e23bdb17aa09","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SH6mEmHrcmJHuU6FYWDPCC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MultiEcuScan vLinker FS STN1170 baud rate 115200 500000 settings AlfaOBD adapter\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Ordered a vGate vLinker MC+\",\"url\":\"https://www.jeepcherokeeclub.com/threads/ordered-a-vgate-vlinker-mc.249899/page-3\"},{\"title\":\"STN1170 Multiprotocol OBD to UART Interpreter Datasheet\",\"url\":\"https://www.scantool.net/downloads/132/stn1170-ds.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"1. Configuring connection to interface\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaobd.com/AlfaOBD_Android_Help.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"wired usb to OBDII dongle for PCM Hammer - LS1TECH - Camaro and Firebird Forum Discussion\",\"url\":\"https://ls1tech.com/forums/pcm-diagnostics-tuning/1984008-wired-usb-obdii-dongle-pcm-hammer.html\"},{\"title\":\"vLinker FS USB\",\"url\":\"https://vgatemall.com/products-detail/i-19/\"},{\"title\":\"Vlinker FS Baudrate - FORScan forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.forscan.org/viewtopic.php?t=23037\"},{\"title\":\"Ordered a vGate vLinker MC+\",\"url\":\"https://www.jeepcherokeeclub.com/threads/ordered-a-vgate-vlinker-mc.249899/\"},{\"title\":\"Problem with Obdlink multiecuscan - MHH AUTO - Page 1\",\"url\":\"https://mhhauto.com/Thread-Problem-with-Obdlink-multiecuscan\"},{\"title\":\"‭OBDLink‬‭®‬‭Family‬ ‭Reference and‬ ‭Programming Manual‬ ‭(FRPM)‬\",\"url\":\"https://www.scantool.net/scantool/downloads/678/obdlink_frpm_e.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Switching Communication Baud Rate\",\"url\":\"https://www.scantool.net/blog/switching-communication-baud-rate/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding the MultiEcuScan vLinker FS STN1170 baud rate settings and AlfaOBD adapter:\n\n## STN1170 Chip and Baud Rate Capabilities\n\nThe STN1170 supports UART interface with baud rates from 38 bps to 10 Mbps, which means it can technically handle both 115200 and 500000 baud rates you mentioned.\n\n## vLinker FS Baud Rate Settings\n\nvLinker FS requires firmware higher than v2.2.91.beta1 to change baud rates, and if the firmware is lower than this version, the baud rate will return to the factory setting of 115200 bps after restart. There is an official utility available for changing the baudrate of vLinker FS.\n\n## Compatibility with AlfaOBD\n\nThe STN1170 is fully compatible with the ELM327/329 AT command set, which is why you can use the MX+ (or MC+) with AlfaOBD or any app that supports the ELM327. Additionally, the vLinker FS works with both FORscan and AlfaOBD.\n\n## Default Settings\n\nThe default UART setting for USB OBDLink adapters is 115200 bps, which appears to be the standard factory setting for these adapters.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"089ed737-3816-4669-9889-9a9773355bb4","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:09:43.119Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"MultiEcuScan vLinker FS STN1170 baud rate 115200 500000 settings AlfaOBD adapter","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01U9HwUVwhWsu4KjsT3C7x16","content":[{"title":"Ordered a vGate vLinker MC+","url":"https://www.jeepcherokeeclub.com/threads/ordered-a-vgate-vlinker-mc.249899/page-3"},{"title":"STN1170 Multiprotocol OBD to UART Interpreter Datasheet","url":"https://www.scantool.net/downloads/132/stn1170-ds.pdf"},{"title":"1. Configuring connection to interface","url":"https://www.alfaobd.com/AlfaOBD_Android_Help.pdf"},{"title":"wired usb to OBDII dongle for PCM Hammer - LS1TECH - Camaro and Firebird Forum Discussion","url":"https://ls1tech.com/forums/pcm-diagnostics-tuning/1984008-wired-usb-obdii-dongle-pcm-hammer.html"},{"title":"vLinker FS USB","url":"https://vgatemall.com/products-detail/i-19/"},{"title":"Vlinker FS Baudrate - FORScan forum","url":"https://forum.forscan.org/viewtopic.php?t=23037"},{"title":"Ordered a vGate vLinker MC+","url":"https://www.jeepcherokeeclub.com/threads/ordered-a-vgate-vlinker-mc.249899/"},{"title":"Problem with Obdlink multiecuscan - MHH AUTO - Page 1","url":"https://mhhauto.com/Thread-Problem-with-Obdlink-multiecuscan"},{"title":"‭OBDLink‬‭®‬‭Family‬ ‭Reference and‬ ‭Programming Manual‬ ‭(FRPM)‬","url":"https://www.scantool.net/scantool/downloads/678/obdlink_frpm_e.pdf"},{"title":"Switching Communication Baud Rate","url":"https://www.scantool.net/blog/switching-communication-baud-rate/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found regarding the MultiEcuScan vLinker FS STN1170 baud rate settings and AlfaOBD adapter:\n\n## STN1170 Chip and Baud Rate Capabilities\n\nThe STN1170 supports UART interface with baud rates from 38 bps to 10 Mbps, which means it can technically handle both 115200 and 500000 baud rates you mentioned.\n\n## vLinker FS Baud Rate Settings\n\nvLinker FS requires firmware higher than v2.2.91.beta1 to change baud rates, and if the firmware is lower than this version, the baud rate will return to the factory setting of 115200 bps after restart. There is an official utility available for changing the baudrate of vLinker FS.\n\n## Compatibility with AlfaOBD\n\nThe STN1170 is fully compatible with the ELM327/329 AT command set, which is why you can use the MX+ (or MC+) with AlfaOBD or any app that supports the ELM327. Additionally, the vLinker FS works with both FORscan and AlfaOBD.\n\n## Default Settings\n\nThe default UART setting for USB OBDLink adapters is 115200 bps, which appears to be the standard factory setting for these adapters."],"durationSeconds":6.793412500143051,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"55d76961-5815-4dbe-900f-2541ff636f4f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssist