{"parentUuid":"940d6666-2f24-4ef2-945e-804cf6b77054","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"a1bf9e23bdb17aa09","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017mBkC2dPfCJoqAyczyyCcq","type":"tool_result","content":"# STN Baud Rate Commands\n\n## Method 1: STSBR (Recommended for firmware v2.0.1+)\n\n**Commands:**\n- `STSBR [baud_rate]` - Set temporary baud rate\n- `STWBR` - Save the new rate permanently\n\n**Syntax example:** `STSBR 38400`\n\n**Host procedure:**\n1. Connect at current speed (typically 115200 bps)\n2. Issue STSBR command with desired rate\n3. \"Switch the terminal emulator to the new baud rate\"\n4. Send `STI` to verify connection; expect response like `\"STN1101 v2.1.0\"`\n5. Execute `STWBR` to persist the change\n\n## Method 2: AT PP 0C (Works on older firmware v1.1.0+)\n\n**Command sequence:**\n```\nATPP 0C SV [xx]\nATPP 0C ON\nATZ\n```\n\n**Common baud rate values:**\n- 38400 bps = `68`\n- 115200 bps = `23`\n- 230400 bps = `11`\n\n**Host procedure:**\n1. Connect at current baud rate\n2. Enter three commands above with appropriate hex value\n3. \"Switch the terminal emulator to the new baud rate\"\n4. Send `ATI` to test; expect `\"ELM327 v1.3a\"`\n\n**Caution:** This method \"allows the baud rate to be set to a value not supported by the communication channel.\""}]},"uuid":"5912bcd7-f038-4ca0-a7d4-865465a3d687","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:09:54.604Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":88681,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# STN Baud Rate Commands\n\n## Method 1: STSBR (Recommended for firmware v2.0.1+)\n\n**Commands:**\n- `STSBR [baud_rate]` - Set temporary baud rate\n- `STWBR` - Save the new rate permanently\n\n**Syntax example:** `STSBR 38400`\n\n**Host procedure:**\n1. Connect at current speed (typically 115200 bps)\n2. Issue STSBR command with desired rate\n3. \"Switch the terminal emulator to the new baud rate\"\n4. Send `STI` to verify connection; expect response like `\"STN1101 v2.1.0\"`\n5. Execute `STWBR` to persist the change\n\n## Method 2: AT PP 0C (Works on older firmware v1.1.0+)\n\n**Command sequence:**\n```\nATPP 0C SV [xx]\nATPP 0C ON\nATZ\n```\n\n**Common baud rate values:**\n- 38400 bps = `68`\n- 115200 bps = `23`\n- 230400 bps = `11`\n\n**Host procedure:**\n1. Connect at current baud rate\n2. Enter three commands above with appropriate hex value\n3. \"Switch the terminal emulator to the new baud rate\"\n4. Send `ATI` to test; expect `\"ELM327 v1.3a\"`\n\n**Caution:** This method \"allows the baud rate to be set to a value not supported by the communication channel.\"","durationMs":6121,"url":"https://www.scantool.net/blog/switching-communication-baud-rate/"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e369bd5d-ad1c-4da1-874c-c97b03ee3666","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"940d6666-2f24-4ef2-945e-804cf6b77054","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
