{"parentUuid":"e0f8446a-3402-476d-a392-f5a10718b79f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"102df512-2a44-48db-815c-5b3ee98b0908","agentId":"a1bf9e23bdb17aa09","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S7vmiTZxgYyUUD7KVgDQx2","type":"tool_result","content":"=== check_live ===\nchecks run: 177\r\nall green\r\n=== check_live_data ===\nchecks run: 88\r\nall green\r\n=== check_active_probe ===\nchecks run: 23\r\nall green\r\n=== check_fullscan ===\nchecks run: 222\r\nall green\r\n=== check_coverage ===\nchecks run: 126\r\nFAILURES: 2\r\n  - untarget clears STN pass filters -- ['ATE0', 'ATL0', 'ATS0', 'ATH1', 'ATAT1', 'ATCAF1', 'STP 33', 'STCMM 1', 'ATSH7DF', 'ATCRA', 'ATSH7DF', 'STFAP 1,7DF,FFFFFFFF']\r\n  - untarget clears STN pass filters on the verified 29-bit route too -- ['ATE0', 'ATL0', 'ATS0', 'ATH1', 'ATAT1', 'ATCAF1', 'STP 34', 'STCMM 1', 'ATCP18', 'ATSHDB33F1', 'ATSTFF', 'ATCRA', 'ATCP18', 'ATSHDB33F1', 'ATSTFF', 'STFAP 1,DB33F1,FFFFFFFF']\r\n=== check_live_readiness ===\n  [ok] the demo readiness observation round-trips through the store\r\n  [ok] ...but is not from the car, however complete its monitors claim to be\r\n  [ok] no system is VERIFIED_CLEAN from a demo-only observation (the demo readiness row above must not have promoted anything)\r\n\r\nall 41 checks passed\r\n=== check_systems_live ===\n  [ok] the new code maps to the ignition system\r\n  [ok] the new code's since is the poller's own first_seen timestamp\r\n  [ok] P0304 still appears exactly once on a second poll, not twice\r\n\r\nall 22 checks passed\r\n=== check_detail ===\nchecks run: 20\r\nall green\r\n=== check_module_codes ===\n63/63 checks passed\r\n=== check_readall ===\nchecks run: 61\r\nall green\r\n=== check_learn ===\nchecks run: 61\r\nall green\r\n=== check_clear ===\nchecks run: 18\r\nall green\r\n=== check_actuate ===\nchecks run: 62\r\nall green\r\n=== check_buscapture ===\nchecks run: 44\r\nall green","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c92d9e47-4841-4d97-9fbf-00d6e046f2af","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:19:41.663Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== check_live ===\nchecks run: 177\r\nall green\r\n=== check_live_data ===\nchecks run: 88\r\nall green\r\n=== check_active_probe ===\nchecks run: 23\r\nall green\r\n=== check_fullscan ===\nchecks run: 222\r\nall green\r\n=== check_coverage ===\nchecks run: 126\r\nFAILURES: 2\r\n  - untarget clears STN pass filters -- ['ATE0', 'ATL0', 'ATS0', 'ATH1', 'ATAT1', 'ATCAF1', 'STP 33', 'STCMM 1', 'ATSH7DF', 'ATCRA', 'ATSH7DF', 'STFAP 1,7DF,FFFFFFFF']\r\n  - untarget clears STN pass filters on the verified 29-bit route too -- ['ATE0', 'ATL0', 'ATS0', 'ATH1', 'ATAT1', 'ATCAF1', 'STP 34', 'STCMM 1', 'ATCP18', 'ATSHDB33F1', 'ATSTFF', 'ATCRA', 'ATCP18', 'ATSHDB33F1', 'ATSTFF', 'STFAP 1,DB33F1,FFFFFFFF']\r\n=== check_live_readiness ===\n  [ok] the demo readiness observation round-trips through the store\r\n  [ok] ...but is not from the car, however complete its monitors claim to be\r\n  [ok] no system is VERIFIED_CLEAN from a demo-only observation (the demo readiness row above must not have promoted anything)\r\n\r\nall 41 checks passed\r\n=== check_systems_live ===\n  [ok] the new code maps to the ignition system\r\n  [ok] the new code's since is the poller's own first_seen timestamp\r\n  [ok] P0304 still appears exactly once on a second poll, not twice\r\n\r\nall 22 checks passed\r\n=== check_detail ===\nchecks run: 20\r\nall green\r\n=== check_module_codes ===\n63/63 checks passed\r\n=== check_readall ===\nchecks run: 61\r\nall green\r\n=== check_learn ===\nchecks run: 61\r\nall green\r\n=== check_clear ===\nchecks run: 18\r\nall green\r\n=== check_actuate ===\nchecks run: 62\r\nall green\r\n=== check_buscapture ===\nchecks run: 44\r\nall green","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_experience_page.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1,"newLines":7,"lines":[" \"\"\"Checks for the \"Others' experience\" feature: cuore/services/experience_bridge.py,"," cuore/api/experience.py, and the _experience.html card included on code.html,","-vehicle.html (dossier open-work), maintenance.html, service_hub.html and","-timeline.html.","+vehicle.html (dossier open-work), maintenance.html, service_hub.html,","+timeline.html and report.html."," "," mes.experience (for_code/for_family/for_job/all) is built in parallel by"," another agent and may not exist yet -- experience_bridge degrades to an"]},{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":6,"newStart":12,"newLines":15,"lines":[" ``cuore.web.experience_globals``'s registered Jinja global calls through to,"," so one patch point covers the API and every page."," ","+Section 5 (added 2026-10-14) covers the driver/mechanic-added half of the","+feature: ``cuore.live.experience_inputs``, the ``/api/experience/{vin}/","+inputs`` round-trip, the merge-with-curated tiering, and the mobile entry","+point on ``m_home.html``. No COM3, no real browser: every row is added with","+``verify=False`` (the API's own ``\"verify\": false``) so :func:`cuore.live.","+experience_inputs.verify_entry` -- which would otherwise shell out to","+headless Edge for a forum URL -- is never invoked; TestClient only, same","+posture as every other ``check_*_page.py`` here.","+"," Run:","     .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_experience_page.py"," \"\"\""]},{"oldStart":36,"oldLines":6,"newStart":45,"newLines":7,"lines":[" from cuore.services import experience_bridge  # noqa: E402"," from cuore.web import experience_globals  # noqa: E402, F401 -- side-effect import, registers the global"," from cuore.api import experience as experience_api  # noqa: E402","+from cuore.live import experience_inputs as experience_inputs_store  # noqa: E402"," "," VIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\""," "]},{"oldStart":236,"oldLines":6,"newStart":246,"newLines":139,"lines":["     check(f\"{script} exits 0\", ok, (proc.stdout[-1200:] + proc.stderr[-1200:]) if not ok else \"\")"," "," ","+# ===========================================================================","+# 5. driver/mechanic-added links: store, merge/tier, API round-trip,","+#    curated read-only, duplicates, edit/delete/undo, mobile entry point","+# ===========================================================================","+","+print(\"=== add a mechanic link: renders with the Mechanic chip + name ===\")","+_patched()","+try:","+    add_resp = client.post(f\"/api/experience/{VIN}/inputs\", json={","+        \"scope\": {\"code\": \"P0456\"}, \"url\": \"https://example.com/mechanic-find\",","+        \"title\": \"Mechanic's own fix video\", \"kind\": \"video\", \"role\": \"mechanic\",","+        \"name\": \"Luca\", \"note\": \"this is what fixed it\", \"rating\": \"helped\",","+        \"verify\": False})","+    check(\"add: 200\", add_resp.status_code == 200, add_resp.text)","+    mech_row = add_resp.json()","+    check(\"add: not flagged a duplicate\", not mech_row.get(\"duplicate\"), str(mech_row))","+    mech_id = mech_row[\"id\"]","+","+    code_resp = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/code/P0456\")","+    check(\"code page: Mechanic chip + name render\", \"Mechanic\" in code_resp.text","+          and \"Luca\" in code_resp.text, code_resp.text[:200])","+","+    report_resp = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/report\")","+    check(\"report: mechanic-added link renders with Mechanic chip + name\",","+          \"Mechanic's own fix video\" in report_resp.text and \"Mechanic\" in report_resp.text","+          and \"Luca\" in report_resp.text)","+","+    print(\"=== driver link sorts after mechanic (tiered, not just by score) ===\")","+    driver_resp = client.post(f\"/api/experience/{VIN}/inputs\", json={","+        \"scope\": {\"code\": \"P0456\"}, \"url\": \"https://example.com/driver-find\",","+        \"title\": \"Driver's note\", \"kind\": \"note\", \"role\": \"driver\", \"name\": \"Sam\",","+        \"note\": \"heard this rattle too\", \"rating\": \"helped\", \"verify\": False})","+    check(\"add driver link: 200\", driver_resp.status_code == 200, driver_resp.text)","+    driver_id = driver_resp.json()[\"id\"]","+","+    merged = experience_bridge.links_for(code=\"P0456\", vin=VIN)","+    ids_in_order = [l[\"id\"] for l in merged[\"links\"]]","+    check(\"mechanic row present and before driver row\",","+          mech_id in ids_in_order and driver_id in ids_in_order","+          and ids_in_order.index(mech_id) < ids_in_order.index(driver_id), str(ids_in_order))","+    check(\"curated rows (tier 0) all sort ahead of both user rows\",","+          all(ids_in_order.index(l[\"id\"]) < ids_in_order.index(mech_id)","+              for l in merged[\"links\"] if l.get(\"curated\")), str(ids_in_order))","+    check(\"counts tally mechanic/driver separately\",","+          merged[\"counts\"].get(\"mechanic\") == 1 and merged[\"counts\"].get(\"driver\") == 1,","+          str(merged[\"counts\"]))","+","+    print(\"=== edit changes the note, with an audit entry ===\")","+    edit_resp = client.patch(f\"/api/experience/{VIN}/inputs/{mech_id}\",","+                             json={\"by_role\": \"mechanic\", \"by_name\": \"Luca\",","+                                   \"note\": \"updated: torqued the fitting too\"})","+    check(\"edit: 200\", edit_resp.status_code == 200, edit_resp.text)","+    after_edit = experience_bridge.list_inputs(VIN)[\"inputs\"]","+    edited_row = next((r for r in after_edit if r[\"id\"] == mech_id), None)","+    check(\"edit: note actually changed\", edited_row is not None","+          and edited_row[\"note\"] == \"updated: torqued the fitting too\", str(edited_row))","+    check(\"edit: audit entry recorded who/when/what changed\",","+          edited_row is not None and len(edited_row.get(\"audit\") or []) == 1","+          and edited_row[\"audit\"][0][\"by\"][\"role\"] == \"mechanic\"","+          and \"note\" in edited_row[\"audit\"][0][\"changes\"], str(edited_row))","+","+    print(\"=== delete + undo ===\")","+    del_resp = client.delete(f\"/api/experience/{VIN}/inputs/{driver_id}\")","+    check(\"delete: 200\", del_resp.status_code == 200, del_resp.text)","+    after_delete = experience_bridge.list_inputs(VIN)[\"inputs\"]","+    check(\"delete: row no longer in the default (non-deleted) list\",","+          all(r[\"id\"] != driver_id for r in after_delete), str(after_delete))","+    restore_resp = client.post(f\"/api/experience/{VIN}/inputs/{driver_id}/restore\")","+    check(\"undo: restore 200\", restore_resp.status_code == 200, restore_resp.text)","+    after_restore = experience_bridge.list_inputs(VIN)[\"inputs\"]","+    check(\"undo: row is back\", any(r[\"id\"] == driver_id for r in after_restore), str(after_restore))","+","+    print(\"=== duplicate URL is flagged, not silently re-added ===\")","+    dup_resp = client.post(f\"/api/experience/{VIN}/inputs\", json={","+        \"scope\": {\"code\": \"P0456\"}, \"url\": \"https://example.com/mechanic-find\",","+        \"kind\": \"video\", \"role\": \"driver\", \"verify\": False})","+    check(\"duplicate: flagged with the existing row's attribution\", dup_resp.status_code == 200","+          and dup_resp.json().get(\"duplicate\") is True","+          and (dup_resp.json().get(\"existing\") or {}).get(\"id\") == mech_id, dup_resp.text)","+    confirm_resp = client.post(f\"/api/experience/{VIN}/inputs\", json={","+        \"scope\": {\"code\": \"P0456\"}, \"url\": \"https://example.com/mechanic-find\",","+        \"kind\": \"video\", \"role\": \"driver\", \"verify\": False, \"confirm_duplicate\": True})","+    check(\"duplicate: confirm_duplicate=true adds it anyway\", confirm_resp.status_code == 200","+          and not confirm_resp.json().get(\"duplicate\"), confirm_resp.text)","+","+    print(\"=== curated row stays uneditable (no Edit/Delete; Flag offered instead) ===\")","+    curated_id = next(l[\"id\"] for l in merged[\"links\"] if l.get(\"curated\"))","+    curated_page = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/code/P0456\")","+    check('curated row gets \"Flag as wrong/outdated\", not Edit/Delete',","+          f'data-exp-flag=\"{curated_id}\"' in curated_page.text","+          and f'data-exp-edit=\"{curated_id}\"' not in curated_page.text","+          and f'data-exp-delete=\"{curated_id}\"' not in curated_page.text)","+    # curated ids were never written via add_input (they come from","+    # mes.experience, read-only), so edit_input must refuse one outright --","+    # that refusal, not any UI affordance, is what actually keeps a","+    # curated row uneditable.","+    try:","+        experience_inputs_store.edit_input(curated_id, by_role=\"owner\", note=\"nope\")","+        check(\"curated id rejected by edit_input\", False, \"no exception raised\")","+    except ValueError:","+        check(\"curated id rejected by edit_input\", True)","+","+    print(\"=== flag + worked tick round-trip against a curated id ===\")","+    flag_resp = client.post(f\"/api/experience/links/{curated_id}/flag\",","+                            json={\"by_role\": \"owner\", \"note\": \"canister P/N changed since\",","+                                  \"flag_kind\": \"outdated\"})","+    check(\"flag curated row: 200\", flag_resp.status_code == 200, flag_resp.text)","+    check(\"flag recorded against the curated id\",","+          len(experience_inputs_store.flags_for(curated_id)) == 1)","+    worked_resp = client.post(f\"/api/experience/links/{mech_id}/worked\",","+                              json={\"by_role\": \"mechanic\", \"job_ref\": \"P0456 EVAP smoke test\"})","+    check(\"worked tick: 200\", worked_resp.status_code == 200, worked_resp.text)","+    check(\"worked tick recorded against the mechanic row\",","+          len(experience_inputs_store.worked_for(mech_id)) == 1)","+","+    print(\"=== export for curation review ===\")","+    export_resp = client.get(f\"/api/experience/{VIN}/inputs/export\")","+    check(\"export: 200\", export_resp.status_code == 200, export_resp.text)","+    export_rows = export_resp.json().get(\"export\") or []","+    check(\"export: the helped mechanic row is offered for curation review\",","+          any(r.get(\"found_by\", {}).get(\"role\") == \"mechanic\" for r in export_rows),","+          str(export_rows))","+finally:","+    _unpatched()","+","+print(\"=== mobile entry point: m_home.html renders the add form ===\")","+mobile_resp = client.get(f\"/m/{VIN}\")","+check(\"mobile home: 200\", mobile_resp.status_code == 200, str(mobile_resp.status_code))","+check('mobile home: \"+ Add what you found\" card renders, wired to experience.js',","+      \"data-exp-add-form\" in mobile_resp.text and \"data-exp-card\" in mobile_resp.text","+      and \"experience.js\" in mobile_resp.text)","+","+"," print()"," if failures:","     print(f\"{len(failures)}/{checks} check(s) failed:\")"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\MES_VS_CUORE_CAPABILITY_2026-10-14.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":157,"lines":["+# MES vs. CUORE: what each can access/modify/service, and what closes the gap","+","+**Date:** 2026-10-14. **Scope:** Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (Giorgio","+platform, GME engine family) -- the platform this repo's own knowledge","+tables (`mes.mechanic_tests`, `mes.known_good`, `mes.systems`) are built","+for. **Method:** multiecuscan.net's own supported-vehicle listing and","+support forum, owner-community writeups (giuliaforums.com,","+stelvioforum.com, giuliatech.com, alfaowner.com, mhhauto.com), and a","+read-only pass over the local install at","+`C:\\Program Files (x86)\\MultiEcuScan` -- its `Lang\\English.txt` UI string","+table (534 entries, the same source `MES_CAPABILITY_GAPS.md`'s 2026-08-27","+pass used) and its own FES session logs. The ECU database itself is","+encrypted and was not touched, per standing instruction.","+","+This doc answers one question: **where is MES the better tool today, where","+is CUORE, and for every MES-only function, what is the safe way to close","+the gap** -- read it into CUORE when a sourced DID exists, otherwise hand","+the technician to MES (or, twice below, to the car's own menu) with a","+clear card, never a silent HTTP write.","+","+The data half of this doc is `mes-log-mcp/mes/mes_functions.py` -- every","+row below is generated from that module, so the two can never drift out of","+sync. Companion reading: `MES_CAPABILITY_GAPS.md` (2026-08-27, the inverse","+question -- what MES *cannot* do) and `MES_INTEGRATION_SURFACE.md`.","+","+## The three-tier closure rule","+","+1. **Read-side, DID exists** -- wire it into `mes_bridge`/`live_obs` like","+  every other channel. Nothing in the table below needs this tier; where","+  CUORE is only \"partial\", the missing half is a channel with no public","+  DID (tier 2).","+2. **Read-side, no DID** -- \"needs DID definition (TechAuthority /","+  learn)\". CUORE does not invent a PID/DID; it stays honestly partial","+  until one is sourced or learned (`obd2.learn_correlate`).","+3. **Write-side** (actuator/adjustment/coding) -- CUORE **never** performs","+  these over HTTP. The few actuator tests already in","+  `mes.mechanic_tests` (e.g. `esim_commanded_vent_test`) are MCP-only,","+  gated on the `ACTUATE ECM <name>` consent phrase. Every other write in","+  this table has no MCP tool at all today -- for those, the only safe","+  path is a **handoff card** (`cuore.services.mes_handoff_bridge`, this","+  pass) pointing the technician at MES (or the car's own menu, for the","+  one exception below).","+","+## The capability matrix","+","+| id | module | kind | MES | CUORE today | menu path (abridged) | confidence |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| all_module_scan | ALL (CAN-C/IHS/CH) | read | yes | yes -- cuore.live.fullscan.run over the  | main toolbar -> Scan vehicle (sweeps every module MES has a database entry for, across ... | CONFIRMED |","+| module_info_identity | ALL | read | yes | partial -- mes.modules/read_module_ident | each module's own screen -> Info tab (ECU part number, HW/SW version, calibration ID) | CONFIRMED |","+| live_parameters | ALL | read | yes | partial -- CUORE's live_obs/channels.py  | each module's own screen -> Parameters tab | CORROBORATED |","+| graphs_recording_csv | ALL | read | yes | no -- CUORE has no equivalent graph/reco | Parameters tab -> graph icon, then Record (writes a .csv under MES's configured Export ... | CORROBORATED |","+| freeze_frames_per_module | ALL | read | yes | partial -- cuore.live.obd read_freeze_fr | each module's own screen -> DTC EX tab | CONFIRMED |","+| esim_commanded_vent_test | Engine/ECM (EVAP) | actuator | yes -- Actuators tab (or wiTEC | no -- MCP-only via obd2.run_actuator wit | Engine -> ECM -> Actuators tab -> ESIM / purge solenoid vent command | CORROBORATED |","+| turbo_boost_waste_gate_actuator | Engine/ECM (intake/boost) | actuator | yes | no -- no CUORE actuator route for this c | Engine -> ECM -> Actuators tab -> boost control solenoid / waste-gate | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| zf_gear_shift_actuator | Gearbox/ZF Electronic Gear Shift Module | actuator | yes | no -- no OBD-II DID for this actuator; M | Gearbox -> ZF Electronic Gear Shift Module -> Actuators tab | CONFIRMED |","+| proxi_alignment_952 | Body/BCM (CAN Setup) | adjustment | yes | no -- CUORE never writes PROXI/configura | Body -> CAN Setup / PROXI ALIGNMENT PROCEDURE (952) -- Adjustment tab; Ctrl+Alt+C opens... | CORROBORATED |","+| oil_change_reset_ecm | Engine/ECM (Magneti Marelli IAW 10JA) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side, never over HTTP; MCP-o | Engine -> Magneti Marelli IAW 10JA CF6/EOBD Injection (2.0) -> Adjustments tab -> Oil C... | CORROBORATED |","+| service_interval_reset | Service module (dash/BCM-side) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | Service -> Service Interval Reset -> Adjustments tab -> NEXT SERVICE KM RESET | CORROBORATED |","+| battery_type_registration | Body/BCM (CAN Setup, byte 63) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> PROXI byte 63, bits 0-3 (80Ah 680A / 95Ah 800A ... | CORROBORATED |","+| ibs_battery_sensor_read | Body/BCM (IBS) | read | yes | no -- no CUORE DID for IBS; this is read | Body -> BCM -> Parameters tab -> IBS group (charge status, SoC, SoH) | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| sas_calibration | Chassis/ABS (Continental MK C1) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | ABS -> Continental ABS MK C1 module -> Parameters tab to check 0 deg, then Adjustments ... | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| abs_accel_sensor_calibration | Chassis/ABS (Continental MK C1) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | ABS -> Continental ABS MK C1 module -> Adjustments tab -> accel sensor calibration | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| abs_pressure_sensor_calibration | Chassis/ABS (Continental MK C1) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | ABS -> Continental ABS MK C1 module -> Adjustments tab -> pressure sensor calibration | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| epb_service_mode | Chassis/EPB | adjustment | no -- native infotainment menu | no | NOT in MES, per owner reports -- Settings -> Driver Assistance -> Brake Service on the ... | CORROBORATED |","+| tpms_pressure_threshold | Body/RF Hub | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | Body -> RFHub -> Adjustments tab -> TPMS pressure threshold (MES >=4.7R3) | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| seat_belt_chime_disable | Dashboard/Instrument Panel | coding | yes | no -- CUORE never performs coding writes | Dashboard -> Instrument Panel -> Adjustments tab -> seat belt chime | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| race_mode_dynamic_control_selector | Body/BCM (CAN Setup) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup (Dynamic Control Selector) -> Adjustments tab (MES 4.5+) | CORROBORATED |","+| acc_cruise_enable | Body/BCM (CAN Setup) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> Cruise Control/ACC settings | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| paddle_shifter_logic | Body/BCM (CAN Setup, byte 156) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> PROXI byte 156, bits 4-5 | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| window_comfort_logic | Body/BCM (CAN Setup, byte 58) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> PROXI byte 58, bit 1 | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| after_wipe_logic | Body/BCM (CAN Setup, byte 126) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> PROXI byte 126, bit 5 | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| cornering_lights_enable | Body/BCM (CAN Setup) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> Cornering Lights option | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| tvm_bcm_etm_coding | Body/TVM, BCM, ETM | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | each module's own screen -> Adjustments/Coding tab, per module | SINGLE-SOURCE |","+| coil_actuator_test | Engine/ECM (ignition) | actuator | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only via obd2.run_ | Engine -> ECM -> Actuators tab (string 6001 \"Actuators\") -> ACTUATES THE COIL (string 6... | CONFIRMED |","+| idle_actuator_test | Engine/ECM (throttle/idle) | actuator | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | Engine -> ECM -> Actuators tab -> ACTUATES IDLE ACTUATOR (string 6205); TIMING ACTUATOR... | CONFIRMED |","+| key_rf_learning | Body/BCM (RF Hub, immobiliser) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | Body -> BCM -> Adjustments tab -> key learning procedure (per-prompt: DETECTING KEY, st... | CONFIRMED |","+| dpf_regen | Exhaust/DPF | adjustment | n/a | n/a | n/a on the 2.0T GME -- this is a gasoline engine with no diesel particulate filter; MES... | CONFIRMED |","+| comfort_bus_module_roster | IHS/CH (Magna Q4 transfer case, TRW steering lock, Bosch HALF camera, Bosch DASM radar, ESEM engine sound, TVM torque vectoring) | read | yes | no -- CUORE's OBD-II link has no path to | main toolbar -> Scan vehicle with an A6 cable (or A5 + MES's IHS/CH adapter) reaches th... | CORROBORATED |","+","+31 functions, every row sourced (see `mes_functions.py` for the full","+`source`/`prerequisites`/`record_after` text abridged above). Full detail,","+including the gap-closure path per row, lives in that module --","+`mes.mes_functions.all_functions()` / `.function(id)`.","+","+## Where MES is better today","+","+- **Per-module parameter scaling for TCM/BCM/ABS.** MES's own database","+  carries the named, scaled parameter for modules CUORE has no DID","+  table for at all (IHS/CH comfort bus: BCM, RF Hub, ABS-specific","+  channels beyond the generic OBD-II PID). This is a database-size","+  problem CUORE cannot out-source without the same reverse-engineered","+  DID table MES ships.","+- **Adjustments, coding, and actuator tests.** Every PROXI byte, service","+  reset, calibration and actuator in the matrix above is a live write","+  CUORE deliberately never performs over HTTP. MES (or wiTECH, or the","+  infotainment menu for the one exception) is simply the right tool for","+  these, full stop -- not a gap to close so much as a boundary to respect.","+- **Cable/connection guidance.** MES's own prompts (and the forum","+  threads sourced above) carry the \"which cable, which bus\" knowledge","+  (A5 vs. A6, the gray ABS-specific cable) that a bare OBD-II link has no","+  way to know.","+- **IHS/CH comfort-bus reach.** With an A6 cable MES/wiTECH reaches a","+  roster of modules (Magna Q4 transfer case, TRW steering lock, Bosch","+  HALF/DASM, ESEM, TVM) a CAN-C-only OBD-II link cannot see at all.","+","+## Where CUORE is better today","+","+- **Verdict/evidence gate.** MES shows a code; CUORE's","+  `scan_health.verdict` turns stored/pending/permanent/readiness/Mode 06","+  into one of four honest states (active fault / verified clean /","+  unverified repair / no data) -- MES has no readiness or Mode 06 concept","+  at all (`MES_CAPABILITY_GAPS.md`'s own headline finding, corroborated","+  again by this pass's string-table read: \"Readiness\", \"EOBD\", \"Permanent\"","+  and \"Freeze\" appear zero times in `Lang\\English.txt`).","+- **Mode 06 interpretation.** Confirmed absent from MES; CUORE reads it","+  directly from the car.","+- **Cross-session history and case memory.** `mes.experience`/`mes.cases`","+  carry what happened last time, on this car and on sibling cars of the","+  same model -- MES has no VIN-keyed service history at all.","+- **Hypotheses, reports, mobile, honesty labels.** The job page's","+  hypothesis tracking, the dossier's confidence-labelled findings, and a","+  phone-sized UI are CUORE's own and have no MES equivalent.","+","+## The one deliberately honest exception","+","+`epb_service_mode` is the one row in this table where **MES is not the","+better tool either** -- per owner reports, MES's own \"EPB maintenance","+mode\" menu item does not reliably work; the brake-service retract lives in","+the car's own infotainment (Settings -> Driver Assistance -> Brake","+Service), and MES's only real role afterward is clearing the resulting","+DTC. The handoff card for this one function says so, rather than sending a","+technician to hunt for a working MES menu that multiple owners report","+does not do what it says.","+","+## What this pass built","+","+1. This doc, and its data half, `mes-log-mcp/mes/mes_functions.py`.","+2. `cuore/services/mes_handoff_bridge.py` -- handoff-card lookup","+  (`candidates`/`find_for_test`/`find_for_text`/`card`) plus MES log","+  import (`import_mes_log`/`list_mes_scans`/`health_line`), additive only","+  -- it never touches `cuore.live.scanlog`, `cuore.services.scan_health_bridge`","+  or `mes.scan_health`'s own files, only calls their public functions","+  (`mes.scan_health.verdict`) and keeps its own small ledger","+  (`mes_imports.json`) for MES-sourced scans, clearly tagged","+  `source.kind = \"MES\"` -- never disguised as a live serial read.","+3. `cuore/web/templates/_mes_handoff.html`, included once each from","+  `tests.html` and `job.html` step 6 -- a client-side script that matches","+  the small MES-function catalogue against whatever test rows / checklist","+  steps are already on the page and injects a card, with an \"Import the","+  MES log\" action when the function typically produces one. It never adds","+  a second result-recording control -- the pass/fail buttons and","+  done/outcome checkbox each row already has are reused as-is.","+4. Two additive routes in `cuore/api/tests.py`","+  (`/tests/mes-handoff/candidates`, `/tests/mes-handoff/by-test/{id}`,","+  `/tests/mes-handoff/by-text`, `/tests/{vin}/mes-import`,","+  `/tests/{vin}/mes-scans`).","+5. `cuore/tests/check_mes_handoff.py`."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\_mes_matrix_table.tmp.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":33,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-| id | module | kind | MES | CUORE today | menu path (abridged) | confidence |\r","-|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r","-| all_module_scan | ALL (CAN-C/IHS/CH) | read | yes | yes -- cuore.live.fullscan.run over the  | main toolbar -> Scan vehicle (sweeps every module MES has a database entry for, across ... | CONFIRMED |\r","-| module_info_identity | ALL | read | yes | partial -- mes.modules/read_module_ident | each module's own screen -> Info tab (ECU part number, HW/SW version, calibration ID) | CONFIRMED |\r","-| live_parameters | ALL | read | yes | partial -- CUORE's live_obs/channels.py  | each module's own screen -> Parameters tab | CORROBORATED |\r","-| graphs_recording_csv | ALL | read | yes | no -- CUORE has no equivalent graph/reco | Parameters tab -> graph icon, then Record (writes a .csv under MES's configured Export ... | CORROBORATED |\r","-| freeze_frames_per_module | ALL | read | yes | partial -- cuore.live.obd read_freeze_fr | each module's own screen -> DTC EX tab | CONFIRMED |\r","-| esim_commanded_vent_test | Engine/ECM (EVAP) | actuator | yes -- Actuators tab (or wiTEC | no -- MCP-only via obd2.run_actuator wit | Engine -> ECM -> Actuators tab -> ESIM / purge solenoid vent command | CORROBORATED |\r","-| turbo_boost_waste_gate_actuator | Engine/ECM (intake/boost) | actuator | yes | no -- no CUORE actuator route for this c | Engine -> ECM -> Actuators tab -> boost control solenoid / waste-gate | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| zf_gear_shift_actuator | Gearbox/ZF Electronic Gear Shift Module | actuator | yes | no -- no OBD-II DID for this actuator; M | Gearbox -> ZF Electronic Gear Shift Module -> Actuators tab | CONFIRMED |\r","-| proxi_alignment_952 | Body/BCM (CAN Setup) | adjustment | yes | no -- CUORE never writes PROXI/configura | Body -> CAN Setup / PROXI ALIGNMENT PROCEDURE (952) -- Adjustment tab; Ctrl+Alt+C opens... | CORROBORATED |\r","-| oil_change_reset_ecm | Engine/ECM (Magneti Marelli IAW 10JA) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side, never over HTTP; MCP-o | Engine -> Magneti Marelli IAW 10JA CF6/EOBD Injection (2.0) -> Adjustments tab -> Oil C... | CORROBORATED |\r","-| service_interval_reset | Service module (dash/BCM-side) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | Service -> Service Interval Reset -> Adjustments tab -> NEXT SERVICE KM RESET | CORROBORATED |\r","-| battery_type_registration | Body/BCM (CAN Setup, byte 63) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> PROXI byte 63, bits 0-3 (80Ah 680A / 95Ah 800A ... | CORROBORATED |\r","-| ibs_battery_sensor_read | Body/BCM (IBS) | read | yes | no -- no CUORE DID for IBS; this is read | Body -> BCM -> Parameters tab -> IBS group (charge status, SoC, SoH) | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| sas_calibration | Chassis/ABS (Continental MK C1) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | ABS -> Continental ABS MK C1 module -> Parameters tab to check 0 deg, then Adjustments ... | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| abs_accel_sensor_calibration | Chassis/ABS (Continental MK C1) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | ABS -> Continental ABS MK C1 module -> Adjustments tab -> accel sensor calibration | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| abs_pressure_sensor_calibration | Chassis/ABS (Continental MK C1) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | ABS -> Continental ABS MK C1 module -> Adjustments tab -> pressure sensor calibration | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| epb_service_mode | Chassis/EPB | adjustment | no -- native infotainment menu | no | NOT in MES, per owner reports -- Settings -> Driver Assistance -> Brake Service on the ... | CORROBORATED |\r","-| tpms_pressure_threshold | Body/RF Hub | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | Body -> RFHub -> Adjustments tab -> TPMS pressure threshold (MES >=4.7R3) | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| seat_belt_chime_disable | Dashboard/Instrument Panel | coding | yes | no -- CUORE never performs coding writes | Dashboard -> Instrument Panel -> Adjustments tab -> seat belt chime | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| race_mode_dynamic_control_selector | Body/BCM (CAN Setup) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup (Dynamic Control Selector) -> Adjustments tab (MES 4.5+) | CORROBORATED |\r","-| acc_cruise_enable | Body/BCM (CAN Setup) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> Cruise Control/ACC settings | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| paddle_shifter_logic | Body/BCM (CAN Setup, byte 156) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> PROXI byte 156, bits 4-5 | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| window_comfort_logic | Body/BCM (CAN Setup, byte 58) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> PROXI byte 58, bit 1 | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| after_wipe_logic | Body/BCM (CAN Setup, byte 126) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> PROXI byte 126, bit 5 | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| cornering_lights_enable | Body/BCM (CAN Setup) | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | Body -> CAN Setup -> Adjustments tab -> Cornering Lights option | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| tvm_bcm_etm_coding | Body/TVM, BCM, ETM | coding | yes | no -- coding write; MCP-only with consen | each module's own screen -> Adjustments/Coding tab, per module | SINGLE-SOURCE |\r","-| coil_actuator_test | Engine/ECM (ignition) | actuator | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only via obd2.run_ | Engine -> ECM -> Actuators tab (string 6001 \"Actuators\") -> ACTUATES THE COIL (string 6... | CONFIRMED |\r","-| idle_actuator_test | Engine/ECM (throttle/idle) | actuator | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | Engine -> ECM -> Actuators tab -> ACTUATES IDLE ACTUATOR (string 6205); TIMING ACTUATOR... | CONFIRMED |\r","-| key_rf_learning | Body/BCM (RF Hub, immobiliser) | adjustment | yes | no -- write-side; MCP-only with consent | Body -> BCM -> Adjustments tab -> key learning procedure (per-prompt: DETECTING KEY, st... | CONFIRMED |\r","-| dpf_regen | Exhaust/DPF | adjustment | n/a | n/a | n/a on the 2.0T GME -- this is a gasoline engine with no diesel particulate filter; MES... | CONFIRMED |\r","-| comfort_bus_module_roster | IHS/CH (Magna Q4 transfer case, TRW steering lock, Bosch HALF camera, Bosch DASM radar, ESEM engine sound, TVM torque vectoring) | read | yes | no -- CUORE's OBD-II link has no path to | main toolbar -> Scan vehicle with an A6 cable (or A5 + MES's IHS/CH adapter) reaches th... | CORROBORATED |"]}],"deleted":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_experience_page.py","C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\MES_VS_CUORE_CAPABILITY_2026-10-14.md","C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\_mes_matrix_table.tmp.md"],"shared":true}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d75876f1-2894-404a-969d-4a439aa1a735","context":{