{"parentUuid":"6537537b-271f-446a-a98f-9632ac3ff17f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1bf9e23bdb17aa09","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg24hZyh4butED9NvyUrV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0197pYYX5wpS7vKiomWtXniK","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Done. Commit 3883c5a pushed to github/main (bea37c9..3883c5a).\n\n**Review doc**: docs/research/OBD_CONNECTIVITY_REVIEW_2026-10-14.md — covers the current path (vLinker FS r2/STN1170 @115200, per-op session open, 29-bit addressing, the STFAC/STCFCPA filter issue, SGW behaviour), tonight's audit-log timings (read_pid sessions ~0.32-1.35s; module_identity ECM/TCM/BCM/IPC 2.45/1.33/5.22/5.21s; discover can_c 75.6s for 253 targets/0 hits; a live_session that ended in a Windows \"Access is denied\" ClearCommError), a comparison table vs MES/wiTECH-AutoAuth/AlfaOBD/native-CAN (confirmed from the actual MES registry: Interface 0 Port Speed is 115200 on COM3 tonight — CUORE isn't behind MES on baud), and a cost/benefit recommendations table.\n\n**Implemented (transport.py, stream.py, poller.py, uds.py — all additive, behaviour-preserving by default)**:\n- `Session.query_pids()` (transport.py:140) — Mode 01 multi-PID batching (≤6/request) with automatic per-PID fallback; generalizes the poller's existing `_poll_pids` logic as a reusable session primitive.\n- `uds.sweep_bus_full()` (uds.py:122) — DTCs + identity + one DID per module inside ONE held session, vs. fullscan's current 3 session-opens per module.\n- `AdapterLink.raised_baud()` (transport.py:628) — opt-in (`CUORE_ADAPTER_BAUD`, off by default), self-reverting `STSBR` UART raise; added `Stream.supports_set_baud` so it's never sent to a transport that can't follow. Wired into poller.py's hot loop as a no-op-by-default wrapper.\n- Probe-based pass-filter restore in `Session.untarget()` — off by default (`CUORE_PASS_FILTER_PROBE`); only bypasses the proven `STCFCPC`+`STP`-reissue path when an `STFAP` probe confirms support.\n- Explicit ISO-TP flow control (`ATFCSH`/`ATFCSD300000`/`ATFCSM1`) added for 29-bit STN targets in `target_raw()`.\n\n**fullscan.py/ops.py were not edited** (outside this task's ownership) — the PID-snapshot loop and per-module sweep are left as recommendations in §4 of the doc for their owner to wire up, with before/after estimates (≈4-10× fewer round trips for the snapshot; ~2-5s + fewer port-churn failure points for the module sweep).\n\n**Testing**: new `cuore/tests/check_transport_perf.py` (46 checks, all green, no COM3). Also ran check_live.py (177), check_active_probe.py (23), check_fullscan.py (222), check_coverage.py (126), check_live_data.py (88), check_perf.py, obd2-mcp/tests (all green) — all as requested. One pre-existing, unrelated failure surfaced in a full-repo sweep: check_dossier_view.py (\"verdict cleared_at is 2026-09-29 -- 2026-10-08\") — confirmed via `git status`/`git diff` that this file and its underlying service are untouched by me and already had uncommitted changes from other work before I started; not something I introduced or am scoped to fix.\n\nOne implementation note worth flagging: my first pass at the pass-filter probe broke check_coverage.py's exact-wire-sequence regression test because its fake adapter answers \"OK\" to any AT/ST command, indistinguishable from real STFAP support — I fixed this by making the probe strictly opt-in via env var rather than auto-detected, which also fully restored that test to green.\n\nCommit hash: 3883c5a."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1544,"cache_read_input_tokens":304575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1544,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0197pYYX5wpS7vKiomWtXniK":{"message":"Done. Commit 3883c5a pushed to github/main (bea37c9..3883c5a).\n\n**Review doc**: docs/research/OBD_CONNECTIVITY_REVIEW_2026-10-14.md — covers the current path (vLinker FS r2/STN1170 @115200, per-op session open, 29-bit addressing, the STFAC/STCFCPA filter issue, SGW behaviour), tonight's audit-log timings (read_pid sessions ~0.32-1.35s; module_identity ECM/TCM/BCM/IPC 2.45/1.33/5.22/5.21s; discover can_c 75.6s for 253 targets/0 hits; a live_session that ended in a Windows \"Access is denied\" ClearCommError), a comparison table vs MES/wiTECH-AutoAuth/AlfaOBD/native-CAN (confirmed from the actual MES registry: Interface 0 Port Speed is 115200 on COM3 tonight — CUORE isn't behind MES on baud), and a cost/benefit recommendations table.\n\n**Implemented (transport.py, stream.py, poller.py, uds.py — all additive, behaviour-preserving by default)**:\n- `Session.query_pids()` (transport.py:140) — Mode 01 multi-PID batching (≤6/request) with automatic per-PID fallback; generalizes the poller's existing `_poll_pids` logic as a reusable session primitive.\n- `uds.sweep_bus_full()` (uds.py:122) — DTCs + identity + one DID per module inside ONE held session, vs. fullscan's current 3 session-opens per module.\n- `AdapterLink.raised_baud()` (transport.py:628) — opt-in (`CUORE_ADAPTER_BAUD`, off by default), self-reverting `STSBR` UART raise; added `Stream.supports_set_baud` so it's never sent to a transport that can't follow. Wired into poller.py's hot loop as a no-op-by-default wrapper.\n- Probe-based pass-filter restore in `Session.untarget()` — off by default (`CUORE_PASS_FILTER_PROBE`); only bypasses the proven `STCFCPC`+`STP`-reissue path when an `STFAP` probe confirms support.\n- Explicit ISO-TP flow control (`ATFCSH`/`ATFCSD300000`/`ATFCSM1`) added for 29-bit STN targets in `target_raw()`.\n\n**fullscan.py/ops.py were not edited** (outside this task's ownership) — the PID-snapshot loop and per-module sweep are left as recommendations in §4 of the doc for their owner to wire up, with before/after estimates (≈4-10× fewer round trips for the snapshot; ~2-5s + fewer port-churn failure points for the module sweep).\n\n**Testing**: new `cuore/tests/check_transport_perf.py` (46 checks, all green, no COM3). Also ran check_live.py (177), check_active_probe.py (23), check_fullscan.py (222), check_coverage.py (126), check_live_data.py (88), check_perf.py, obd2-mcp/tests (all green) — all as requested. One pre-existing, unrelated failure surfaced in a full-repo sweep: check_dossier_view.py (\"verdict cleared_at is 2026-09-29 -- 2026-10-08\") — confirmed via `git status`/`git diff` that this file and its underlying service are untouched by me and already had uncommitted changes from other work before I started; not something I introduced or am scoped to fix.\n\nOne implementation note worth flagging: my first pass at the pass-filter probe broke check_coverage.py's exact-wire-sequence regression test because its fake adapter answers \"OK\" to any AT/ST command, indistinguishable from real STFAP support — I fixed this by making the probe strictly opt-in via env var rather than auto-detected, which also fully restored that test to green.\n\nCommit hash: 3883c5a."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f477d8b7-8a47-4183-850a-9713f71a70fc","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg24hZHGZsAhiAAtHm8WG","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5247e60a-fb78-44d6-b1e1-33530f14f254","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:39:21.024Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
