probe confirms support.\n- Explicit ISO-TP flow control (`ATFCSH`/`ATFCSD300000`/`ATFCSM1`) added for 29-bit STN targets in `target_raw()`.\n\n**fullscan.py/ops.py were not edited** (outside this task's ownership) — the PID-snapshot loop and per-module sweep are left as recommendations in §4 of the doc for their owner to wire up, with before/after estimates (≈4-10× fewer round trips for the snapshot; ~2-5s + fewer port-churn failure points for the module sweep).\n\n**Testing**: new `cuore/tests/check_transport_perf.py` (46 checks, all green, no COM3). Also ran check_live.py (177), check_active_probe.py (23), check_fullscan.py (222), check_coverage.py (126), check_live_data.py (88), check_perf.py, obd2-mcp/tests (all green) — all as requested. A full-repo sweep (outside this task's scope) also surfaced two pre-existing/unrelated failures: check_dossier_view.py (\"verdict cleared_at is 2026-09-29 -- 2026-10-08\") and check_job_ux.py — confirmed via `git status`/`git diff` that neither of those files, nor the services behind them, were touched by this work; both already had uncommitted changes from other in-progress work before this task started, so they are not something introduced here or in scope to fix.\n\nOne implementation note worth flagging: my first pass at the pass-filter probe broke check_coverage.py's exact-wire-sequence regression test because its fake adapter answers \"OK\" to any AT/ST command, indistinguishable from real STFAP support — I fixed this by making the probe strictly opt-in via env var rather than auto-detected, which also fully restored that test to green.\n\nCommit hash: 3883c5a."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":307697,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":358,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transfor